// The CELT layer of Opus (RFC 6716, section 4.3): the MDCT codec for music and the upper band
// of hybrid frames. A port of libopus' floating-point decoder (celt_decoder.c, bands.c,
// quant_bands.c, rate.c, vq.c, cwrs.c, laplace.c), for the 48 kHz mode with frames of 2.5 to
// 20 ms. Each frame codes the energy of 21 bands (coarse, fine and final bits), splits the bits
// left among the bands, and codes each band's shape as pulses on a sphere (PVQ), folding the
// spectrum below where no pulses were sent; the inverse MDCT of the spectrum, overlapped with a
// short window, goes through a pitch post-filter and de-emphasis.
//
// Lost frames are not concealed: a damaged or missing frame becomes silence (the caller resets).

import celt_tables as t;
import rangedec as rd;
import std/math;

